To find the total meters Matthew runs in a week, we'll multiply the number of sprints by the distance per sprint and then by the number of times he runs each week.

1. \text{Total sprints per week} = 433 \text{ sprints} \times 309 \text{ times} = 133,797 \text{ sprints}  
2. \text{Total meters per week} = 133,797 \text{ sprints} \times 164 \text{ meters/sprint} = 21,942,708 \text{ meters}  

The information about Matthew's uncle's running shoes is irrelevant to the calculation.

